CLASS com/charlesproxy/export/pcap/class_146 com/charlesproxy/export/pcap/TCPPacket
	COMMENT One IPv4 TCP packet out of a pcap capture. Named by its own exception messages, "TCPPacket sourceAddress invalid length" and "TCPPacket destAddress invalid length".
	COMMENT The flag fields are fixed by PcapFileReader's read order over TCP header byte 13 (CWR, ECE, URG, ACK, PSH, RST, SYN, FIN); only ACK, RST, SYN and FIN are kept. TCPStream's "SYN" debug line confirms syn independently.
	FIELD field_681 timestamp J
	FIELD field_672 sourceAddress [B
	FIELD field_678 destAddress [B
	FIELD field_679 sourcePort I
	FIELD field_674 destPort I
	FIELD field_683 sequenceNumber I
	FIELD field_676 ackNumber I
	FIELD field_677 payload [B
	FIELD field_682 syn Z
	FIELD field_673 ack Z
	FIELD field_684 rst Z
	FIELD field_675 fin Z
	FIELD field_680 normalizedSequenceNumber J
		COMMENT Filled in by TCPStream, not by the reader: the raw sequence number widened past its 32-bit wraparound so it can be used as an absolute offset into the reassembled stream.
	METHOD method_611 getSourceAddress ()Ljava/net/InetAddress;
	METHOD method_610 getDestAddress ()Ljava/net/InetAddress;
